    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe logic itself is in the right place and the refactor to a `while` loop is the correct, idiomatic structure for an \"advance until business day\" rule. The javadoc update is thorough. My one finding is about placement consistency:\n\n- **`PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` breaks the class's established constants convention.** This class groups all its `static final` constants in a dedicated block at the top (`AUDIT`, `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY`, `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY`, `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD` at lines 53\u201373). The new `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` constant is instead declared mid-class at line 542, immediately above `rollToBusinessDay`. A maintainer of this codebase would expect constants in the top block and would look there for them; introducing a one-off constant far down the file makes the constant set harder to discover and inconsistent with the surrounding structure. Move `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` (with its javadoc) up into the existing constants group near line 73.\n\nEverything else \u2014 the immutable `Set.of`, the loop condition, the null guard, the doc wording \u2014 is clean and additive.",
